<title>MOROCCO: King names president of Moroccan supreme court.</title>
<headline>King names president of Moroccan supreme court.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>King Hassan of Morocco appointed Driss Dahak as president of the supreme court on Monday to replace the former president who died last month, the official MAP news agency said.</p>
<p>Dahak, 57, a magistrate and former director of the Moroccan Institute of Judiciary Studies, was appointed during an official ceremony at the royal palace of Rabat, MAP said.</p>
